  "result": "Excellent! All tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added VAT (Value Added Tax) calculation to the invoice system:\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n1. **invoices.js - `invoiceTotals` function**:\n   - Now calculates VAT per line on the amount AFTER discount\n   - VAT is rounded per line using `roundCents`\n   - Invoice VAT is the sum of rounded line VATs (not a percentage of invoice total)\n   - Returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }` where `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n   - All amounts clamped at 0\n\n2. **render.js - `renderInvoiceText` function**:\n   - Added VAT line showing in formatted Euros (only displays if VAT > 0)\n   - VAT line appears just above the Total line\n   - Format: `VAT: \u20acXX.XX`\n\n3. **Tests**: Added 9 comprehensive new tests covering:\n   - VAT calculation with no discount (21%, 9%, 0% rates)\n   - VAT applied to amount after discount\n   - VAT on multiple lines with different rates\n   - VAT with 100% discount (should be 0)\n   - VAT rounded per line (not total)\n   - Total calculations including VAT\n   - Updated 10+ existing tests to include vat field assertions\n   - Updated render tests to account for VAT line in output\n\n**Calculation flow per line**:\n1. Line gross total = qty \u00d7 unitPrice\n2. Line discount = line total \u00d7 discountPercent / 100\n3. Line amount (after discount) = line total - discount\n4. Line VAT = line amount \u00d7 vatRate / 100 (rounded)\n5. Invoice totals = sum of per-line calculations",
